Oh, no, you did.

357
00:20:37,840 --> 00:20:40,877
Half a day is all you need,
but that's not the issue.

358
00:20:40,960 --> 00:20:42,637
For the first half of your journey,

359
00:20:42,720 --> 00:20:46,677
the long poles was recording the
magnetic waves of each destination,

360
00:20:46,760 --> 00:20:49,936
so you were able to navigate
between islands that way.

361
00:20:50,200 --> 00:20:54,077
However, the second half of the Grand
Line won't be so easy to predict.

362
00:20:54,160 --> 00:20:56,317
In addition to the
currents and the weather,

363
00:20:56,400 --> 00:21:01,640
