511
00:29:37,940 --> 00:29:38,770
Uh-huh.

512
00:29:52,260 --> 00:29:54,080
I miss it already!

513
00:29:54,500 --> 00:29:56,680
All those gorgeous mermaids!

514
00:29:57,700 --> 00:30:00,160
Look alive, you guys! Don't goof off!

515
00:30:00,480 --> 00:30:03,833
Once we ascend, who knows what
trouble we might run into?

516
00:30:03,920 --> 00:30:06,697
You remember how scary it was
on the way down, don't you?

517
00:30:06,780 --> 00:30:07,610
Huh?

518
00:30:07,693 --> 00:30:09,697
What's with the weird boxes, Franky?

519
00:30:09,780 --> 00:30:12,251
Those are hollow cubes made out of Banyan.

520
00:30:12,360 --> 00:30:14,007
They're gonna help us float.

521
00:30:15,000 --> 00:30:18,588
I can even adjust the ship's
speed based on how many I throw.

522
00:30:19,300 --> 00:30:20,960
Luffy, what's up?

523
00:30:21,240 --> 00:30:23,200
Once we reach the new world...

524
00:30:25,940 --> 00:30:27,660
Shanks won't be far away.

525
00:30:33,420 --> 00:30:35,280
I hope I see him soon.

526
00:30:36,780 --> 00:30:40,120
In that case, I'll leave this hat to you.

527
00:30:41,220 --> 00:30:43,620
It means more to me than anything else.

528
00:30:44,100 --> 00:30:49,180
I want you to bring this hat back to me,
but not until you become a great pirate.

529
00:30:54,040 --> 00:30:57,720
There is one thing that hurts.

530
00:30:59,080 --> 00:31:03,740
I won't be around to see
you fulfill your dream.

531
00:31:04,260 --> 00:31:05,240
That's fine.

532
00:31:05,600 --> 00:31:06,660
I have faith.

533
00:31:06,780 --> 00:31:08,360
You can do it.

534
00:31:10,080 --> 00:31:11,609
Because you're my brother.

535
00:31:12,440 --> 00:31:14,640
There is yet joy beyond your sorrow.

536
00:31:15,340 --> 00:31:16,900
What's gone may be gone.

537
00:31:17,520 --> 00:31:21,696
But you still have something left in
this world to treasure, don't you?

538
00:31:21,900 --> 00:31:24,429
Let nothing stop you
from reaching the top.

539
00:31:24,860 --> 00:31:25,880
By the way,

540
00:31:26,380 --> 00:31:28,457
I was wondering if you've
ever heard the name

541
00:31:28,540 --> 00:31:31,305
they use for the second
half of the Grand Line.

542
00:31:32,700 --> 00:31:36,880
On the other side of the red line,
at the far reaches of the ocean,

543
00:31:37,180 --> 00:31:40,356
is a place that few pirates
or marines have ever seen.

544
00:31:40,580 --> 00:31:43,600
They call it the New World.

545
00:31:45,240 --> 00:31:46,380
The New World.

546
00:31:49,980 --> 00:31:51,577
There's a new era coming,

547
00:31:51,660 --> 00:31:55,097
and the people who can guide
it are gathering on those seas.

548
00:31:55,180 --> 00:31:59,740
They say the one who can master those
waters will become king of the pirates.

549
00:32:02,520 --> 00:32:04,980
Who knows what's waiting for us up there?

550
00:32:06,620 --> 00:32:08,796
That's the greatest sea in the world!

551
00:32:09,000 --> 00:32:10,100
Took long enough.

552
00:32:10,520 --> 00:32:12,049
I'm ready for some action.

553
00:32:12,240 --> 00:32:13,946
It won't be long now, Laboon.

554
00:32:14,140 --> 00:32:15,700
Just one half to go.

555
00:32:15,900 --> 00:32:18,477
With this new lug pose,
I can take us anywhere.

556
00:32:18,560 --> 00:32:21,097
And wherever we go,
the Snow can handle it.

557
00:32:21,180 --> 00:32:23,517
Don't worry, I'll treat all your injuries!

558
00:32:23,600 --> 00:32:26,541
And as long as I'm around,
you'll never go hungry.

559
00:32:26,800 --> 00:32:28,918
The great Usam's got your back, too!

560
00:32:35,480 --> 00:32:37,617
All right!

561
00:32:37,700 --> 00:32:38,800
Let's go!

562
00:32:51,640 --> 00:32:53,100
New World Waiting!

563
00:32:53,780 --> 00:32:54,610
Yeah!
